# XSH mq_unlink()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Message passing option (MSG). The page lets mq_unlink() return at once or
# wait for the last close, with EINTR if interrupted; tests that unlink a
# queue that is open guard the call with an alarm and are UNRESOLVED if it
# waits. EACCES has no stated condition and is not tested.

assertion  XSH.mq_unlink.001
anchor     functions/mq_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/mq_unlink.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       mq_unlink() of an existing queue returns 0 and the name is gone at
           once, even while a descriptor is open: mq_open() without O_CREAT
           then fails with ENOENT.
test       t/001-removes-name.c

assertion  XSH.mq_unlink.002
anchor     functions/mq_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       After mq_unlink() the name creates a new, empty queue with
           O_CREAT|O_EXCL (no EEXIST) while the old queue lives on,
           with its message, for the descriptor still open.
test       t/002-name-reuse.c

assertion  XSH.mq_unlink.003
anchor     functions/mq_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       Descriptors open when mq_unlink() is called keep sending and
           receiving on the unlinked queue.
test       t/003-descriptors-work.c

assertion  XSH.mq_unlink.004
anchor     functions/mq_unlink.html#ERRORS/ENOENT
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2001
says       mq_unlink() of a name that is not in use fails with ENOENT, and so
           does a second mq_unlink() of a name just removed.
test       t/004-enoent.c

assertion  XSH.mq_unlink.005
anchor     functions/mq_unlink.html#ERRORS/ENAMETOOLONG
class      conditional
when       MSG
since      2008
says       mq_unlink() of a name that mq_open() accepted (the longest of
           4200, 1500, 255 and 100 bytes that it takes) does not fail with
           ENAMETOOLONG and removes the queue.
test       t/005-same-name-accepted.c
